Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:37:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 0078: revF - observe the letterbox fitter's three Output
 writes and the caller's consumption of its Result

The revE session's two new gates (the bake's settings pair, the layer-composition
rect push) both carried the full [1920 888] pair - not the confiner. But the same
session's PB_CALL rows show the game feeding the fitter a (32, 0, 1664, 888)
rect 256 times in one battle, and 888*16/9 = 1578.67 is exactly the confined
width measured on the device: the fitter body's null-rect variant is the float
16:9 clamp (fdiv s3 = W/1.7778, fmul s2 = H*1.7778, fcsel picks the pair). Gate
the fitter's three Output writes (rect path A and B, the float clamp C) and the
caller's Result consumption (the 16 bytes at [x21+0xd0] it ldp's right after the
call): whatever lands at (170, 0, 1749, 888) is the draw rect that confines the
picture, and the cut follows from it.

Generated by Mistral Vibe.
Co-Authored-By: Mistral Vibe <vibe@mistral.ai>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: The pillarbox hunt, revF: revE's two gates both carried the full [1920 888] pair (the bake's settings pair TBK_PAIR, the layer-composition push ELY_RECT - neither confines), while PB_CALL saw the game hand the letterbox fitter a (32, 0, 1664, 888) = 1632x888 rect 256 times in one battle, and 888*16/9 = 1578.67 is exactly the confined width measured on the device; the fitter body's null-rect variant is the float 16:9 clamp. Four more read-only observation gates record the fitter's three Output writes (FIT_A main+0x45f8cc, FIT_B main+0x45f90c, FIT_C main+0x45f968) and the caller's Result consumption (FIT_S main+0x46f2f0, the 16 bytes at [x21+0xd0]); host side dm/host/hle_pillarbox.c (Documents/pillarbox_probe.txt, 60 MB cap)
Issue: mexicanstratocaster/NX2Apple-edgy#1

